From 1b352eae1c0426c9e70e52354095d1e64af50294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:34:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): fire transform_tool_result after post_tool_call
 on the sequential registry path [daveey]

The sequential executor suppresses handle_function_call's inner post_tool_call
and emits it itself after the call returns, but the inner call still ran
transform_tool_result immediately, so on registry tools (terminal, read_file,
...) the transform fired BEFORE post_tool_call. That breaks the hook's
documented contract ("Runs after post_tool_call") and the common plugin
pattern of queueing a hint in post_tool_call and attaching it in
transform_tool_result: the hint landed on the NEXT tool's result.

model_tools gains defer_transform_tool_result_hook(): inside it,
_apply_transform_tool_result_hook queues its call instead of running it. The
sequential registry dispatch wraps handle_function_call in it and
_publish_sequential_result fires the queued transforms right after
emit_post. suppress_post_tool_call_hook(False) (connector batch entries that
own their post) lifts the deferral so those still transform inline. Concurrent
and inline paths already ran post first; the new test pins all four
(sequential/concurrent x registry/inline) and fails before on
sequential-registry only.
